TASK: Rebuild the BlueMind microphone/voice composer flow to behave like a polished native iOS voice input experience.

IMPORTANT:
If there is old/broken voice recording code, outdated web recorder code, duplicated waveform logic, or unstable legacy implementation blocking this behavior, remove/replace it cleanly instead of patching around it.

This should be implemented as a proper iOS-style voice composer state.

==================================================
1. IDLE STATE
==================================================

Normal composer:

[ + ]   Ask anything...   [ mic ]   [ send ]

When user taps the microphone button:
- immediately enter voice recording mode
- do not open a separate page
- do not open a modal
- replace the normal composer contents with the voice UI

==================================================
2. RECORDING STATE
==================================================

While recording, the composer should become:

[ X ]   LIVE WAVEFORM   [ stop ]   [ send ]

Behavior:

LEFT:
X button
- cancels recording immediately
- deletes temporary recording
- exits recording state
- restores the normal text input instantly

CENTER:
Live waveform
- must react to actual microphone amplitude
- quiet voice = small waveform
- louder voice = larger waveform
- update smoothly in real time
- do NOT use a fake looping animation

RIGHT:
Stop button
- square stop icon
- stops recording but does NOT immediately send

Send button
- sends the voice input flow directly to the chat

==================================================
3. CANCEL BEHAVIOR
==================================================

When user taps X:

- stop microphone capture immediately
- discard temporary audio
- remove waveform
- return to the exact normal composer:

[ + ] Ask anything... [ mic ] [ send ]

No loading.
No confirmation dialog.
No leftover waveform.
No stale recording state.

==================================================
4. SEND WHILE RECORDING
==================================================

When user taps SEND while still recording:

1. stop recording
2. process speech recognition
3. convert speech to text
4. send the recognized TEXT as a normal chat message
5. do NOT send an audio bubble
6. preserve the detected spoken language
7. clear voice state
8. return composer to normal

Example:
User speaks Arabic
-> send Arabic text

User speaks Swedish
-> send Swedish text

User speaks English
-> send English text

Do not force one language manually if automatic language detection is available.

==================================================
5. STOP BUTTON BEHAVIOR
==================================================

When user taps STOP:

1. stop recording
2. show a short processing/loading state
3. transcribe the recorded speech to text
4. place the transcribed text into the normal text composer
5. DO NOT send it automatically
6. let the user edit the text
7. user can then press send manually

Desired flow:

Recording
-> tap Stop
-> small loader
-> transcript appears inside input
-> normal composer returns
-> user can edit transcript
-> user sends when ready

==================================================
6. TRANSCRIPTION
==================================================

Speech-to-text must:
- support automatic language detection where possible
- preserve Arabic
- preserve Swedish
- preserve English
- handle mixed-language speech reasonably
- return proper Unicode text
- preserve punctuation where supported

Do not hardcode English.

==================================================
